-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two files whose provenance is UNCONFIRMED
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

    InPlaceEdit.h
    InPlaceEdit.cpp

These deliberately carry NO licence header. They are the only tracked sources
in this repository with no copyright notice of any kind, and they declare a
class, CInPlaceEdit, whose name and shape match a widely circulated public
sample for in-place editing of a CListCtrl subitem. The file is built from
ClassWizard scaffolding (the //{{AFX_VIRTUAL and //{{AFX_MSG markers), which
places at least the skeleton with Microsoft, and nothing in the file records
who wrote the rest.

Asserting copyright over code whose origin cannot be established is worse than
leaving a documented gap, so the licensing sweep skipped them. Before this
repository is published, either establish that the code is ours and apply the
standard header, or replace it - CInPlaceEdit is small and its behaviour is
fully described by CListViewEx, which is the only consumer.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Files that earlier revisions tracked and no longer do
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

None of these needs an exception, because none is distributed any more:

  - TargetcoreMFC.aps and TargetcoreMFC(2026).vcxproj.user were tracked only
    because they predated the .gitignore rules that name them. The first is the
    resource editor's binary cache, regenerated from the .rc; the second is
    per-user IDE settings. Neither is source.
  - (Blocked)P2Peermfc.h, P2PmsgMFC.cpp and P2PmsgMFC.def were AppWizard output
    for a DLL this repository does not build. <ModuleDefinitionFile> is empty in
    all four configurations, so the .def was never read.
  - The earlier-revision sources carrying a bracketed suffix - (SMA), (NLR),
    [NLR], [Discontinued], _NLR - were alternative or superseded copies,
    including the four Ole*Ex[Discontinued] drag-and-drop files that
    COleDropTarget_Ext replaced. None was in the build, none was included by
    anything that was, and nothing outside this repository referenced them.
  - res/P2Properties_Wnd.ico and res/P2Properties_Wnd_hc.ico were unreferenced:
    the resource script loads the .bmp files of those names, never the icons.


